the Solus project is a first person  survival adventure game set on a  deserted alien planet unlike most other  survival games the Solus project is not  a sandbox game with an open world but  rather a more traditional linear  single-player experience with some  survival elements as an experience it's  similar to traditional shooters there's  a linear path through the world with ten  large and complex levels to play through  the story goes that you crash land on an  alien planet every other member of your  crew is dead while exploring the Barons  surroundings you find out that you are  not the first intelligent being to have  set foot here you stumble upon  megalithic buildings similar to ancient  buildings on earth and strangely enough  remains of what appear to be human like  aliens who were they and what brought  about their demise the experience we're  after is one of intense isolation so  this is Latin for a loan the planet is  deserted your crew are dead all of the  aliens on the planet appear to be as  well there are no animals and no life in  general it is totally deserted you are  light-years from any human contact and  there are no other ships that can come  to your rescue if that weren't bad  enough mankind is on the verge of  extinction and you were supposed to be  the last hope for finding a safe haven  to set up a colony now here you are  crash-landed on a small island utterly  isolated utterly alone yet the faith of  mankind rests with you you have no  choice but to survive  you
 

